-- title:
--   Endomorphisms with vanishing linear part factor through Frobenius
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $p$ a prime with $k$ of characteristic $p$, and let $F$ be an $n$-dimensional formal group law over $k$: a family $F_i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n$) of formal power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,n$, with zero constant term, with the coefficient of $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ and of $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$ in $F_i$ equal to $\delta_{ij}$, and satisfying the associativity identity $F(F(X,Y),Z) = F(X,F(Y,Z))$ in the three-fold sum of variable sets. Let $\varphi = (\varphi_i)_{i}$ be a family of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ over $k$ such that each $\varphi_i$ has zero constant coefficient, such that $\varphi_i(F(X,Y)) = F_i(\varphi(X), \varphi(Y))$ for every $i$ (the substitutions being taken with the variables of the two copies of $\varphi$ pushed into the left and right summands respectively), and such that the linear part of $\varphi$ vanishes, i.e. the matrix whose $(i,j)$ entry is the coefficient of the monomial $X_j$ in $\varphi_i$ is the zero matrix. Then there exists a family $\psi = (\psi_i)_i$ of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ over $k$, each with zero constant coefficient, with $\varphi_i = \psi_i(X_1^p, \dots, X_n^p)$ for every $i$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that an endomorphism of a formal group law over a field of characteristic $p$ whose linear part vanishes factors through the Frobenius substitution $X_j \mapsto X_j^p$. It is used in the study of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules, where it yields that the ideal generated by the components of a uniformiser action coincides with the ideal generated by the $p$-th powers of the variables.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_eq_subst_X_pow_of_linearPart_eq_zero.lean

